## Red-test defects (committed Red files, not edited; each one is unsatisfiable by any Green code)
Each defect was proved with a throwaway copy of the test file in __tests__ (named zz-diag-*; deleted, never committed).
In the copies, with only these defects fixed, every other case passed.
- D1 look-decodable-case "ships no upper-case transform": its last assertion expects that decodable.tsx still contains
  toUpperCase. The first assertion of the same case needs no toUpperCase in app or lib. The two contradict.
- D2 look-reader-highlight H1: it asserts frames_run above 100 for each page run. Page 4 has 89 frames at 16 ms.
  No reader can pass. With that one check removed, all 7 highlight cases passed (H1 to H7 incl. 4 phases, 33 words).
- D3 look-word-clip-tap C3: renderPage calls pageBook on the same week object for 8 pages, so page 2 throws a TypeError in the
  test. The last lines compare a clip map built by index with the map built by key, which are equal, and assert they differ.
- D4 look-word-clip-tap C7: the Thai half re-renders after the test installed a resolving play mock. The rejecting mock is not
  installed again, so no alert can show.
- D5 look-word-clip-tap receiver block: walk_not_in_list counts approval.audio.source (a string that ends in a media extension).
  phase3-media-coverage allows the approval, print, and benchmark paths. mediaOf must not list them.
- D6 phase3-audio-seek-stop.test.tsx: the Red commit left the describe "a second word tap replaces the first cut stop (finding F146)"
  with no test. Vitest reports "No test found in suite" and fails the file.
Request to the orchestrator: a Mid Red retry that fixes D1 to D6, then a Green rerun of tasks 1.2, 1.9, and 1.10.
Green expects no more code change: with D1 to D5 fixed in the copies, 12/12 clip cases and 7/7 highlight cases passed.

