## Decisions taken with a default (no question tool; the orchestrator may change them)
- Q-A: Next is disabled on the last page only when the reader has no tiles and no questions (look-feedback needs a disabled Next at 8 / 8;
  phase3-readalong-ui, phase3-reader-end, phase3-adversarial-r2-end-tiles, and phase3-question-screen need the end view). The real page always passes tiles.
- Q-B: only a press on Next holds the page. Previous and a swipe turn at once (look-feedback and phase3-readalong-ui need that).
- Q-C: the client 404 view imports the text from messages/en.json, because the locale layout has no client message provider.
  The server component reads the locale with getLocale and falls back to the routing default.
- Q-D: the word hit area is a pseudo-element that is 0.5 rem higher above and below and 0.25 rem wider on each side.
  A short word keeps a hit area narrower than 44 px, so it cannot take the tap of a neighbour. The browser row tap_target_min_px_player
  (phase3-browser-gate.sh) may measure the word box and report less than 44 px. The browser review decides.
- Q-E: icon.png is the study crest q-crest.svg drawn at 128 px (10215 bytes). The commit body names the source file.
- Q-F: ReaderLabels.playing is optional with a locale default, so the three old tests that build labels without it keep type-checking.
- Q-G: the timeupdate event also moves the highlight (one more trigger of the same function), because phase3-readalong-ui lights a word
  after one timeupdate with no frame. The frame loop of useReadAlong is the main driver.

